# Agent Harness Router — Auto-invocation Rule

> Trigger: When an agent needs to select a model, enforce budget, or capture a useful AI pattern
> This rule is loaded from .cursor/rules/ and is always active.

## When to invoke agent-harness-router

1. **Model selection** — Before calling any LLM API, run:
   ```bash
   node tools/agent-harness-router.js route '{"requiresTools":true,"category":"coding","preference":"balance"}'
   ```
   This enforces the $10/mo budget cap and selects the best model by cost/latency/quality.

2. **Session start** — Automatically runs via `~/.claude/settings.json` SessionStart hook.
   ```bash
   node tools/agent-harness-router.js check --json
   ```

3. **Every user prompt** — Automatically runs via `~/.claude/settings.json` UserPromptSubmit hook.

4. **Useful prompt discovery** — When a prompt/task produces good results, capture it:
   ```bash
   node tools/agent-harness-router.js discover "<prompt>" --model <modelId> --task <taskType> --tags <tag1,tag2>
   ```

## Safety guarantees

- Never captures keystrokes, clicks, or local Mac activity (fail-closed)
- Budget enforcement: $10/mo hard cap, fail-closed
- Secret rejection: blocks AWS keys, GitHub PATs, JWTs, Bearer tokens in discoveries
- Input-capture refusal: blocks Computer History / event_tap / keystroke data
- Third-party models blocked when budget exhausted or sensitive data required

